WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.433
Ally stared at Tina in shock.

2
00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:11.416
"You're Tinakron Beta1P of Astralia, the famous commander of the Astralian fleet?"

3
00:00:11.417 --> 00:00:13.679
"Shh!" Tina whispered.

4
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.728
"A human might hear you. Yes, I was sent to bring you home.

5
00:00:18.729 --> 00:00:25.548
We've been receiving spotty transmissions of your location ever since your escape pod left its mother ship."

6
00:00:25.549 --> 00:00:27.918
Ally narrowed her eyes at Tina.

7
00:00:27.919 --> 00:00:33.365
"Is this a trick? Jorgandians can be very sly."

8
00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:37.335
"I am one hundred percent Astralian."

9
00:00:37.336 --> 00:00:41.677
Tina reached under the collar of her uniform and pulled out a meld medallion.

10
00:00:41.678 --> 00:00:46.179
Removing it, she transformed into her Astralian form.

11
00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:51.827
"Whoa! You are Astralian! Do you have a ship here?"

12
00:00:51.828 --> 00:00:54.744
Tina put her meld medallion back on.

13
00:00:54.745 --> 00:01:02.172
"Of course. My spaceship is at the airport, masked as a small plane.

14
00:01:02.173 --> 00:01:09.898
I was checking on it the other day when you saw me there."

15
00:01:09.899 --> 00:01:14.745
"This is amazing!" Ally cried. "When are we leaving?"

16
00:01:14.746 --> 00:01:18.688
"Shh!" Tina said. "We're leaving soon, but first we—"

17
00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:21.319
"How are my parents?" Ally asked.

18
00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:27.077
"Have they missed me? I bet I'm in big, big trouble for what happened to our pod!"

19
00:01:27.078 --> 00:01:32.639
"Your parents have missed you and are eager for you to return home," Tina said.

20
00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.997
"I hope so," Ally said ruefully.

21
00:01:35.998 --> 00:01:39.339
"I've made so many mistakes."

22
00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.540
Tina patted her on the shoulder.

23
00:01:41.541 --> 00:01:45.020
"Everyone makes mistakes, Allyzooba."

24
00:01:45.021 --> 00:01:48.723
"It sure feels good to hear that," Ally thought.

25
00:01:48.724 --> 00:01:54.078
"Because I don't know how many mistakes I've made since I've been on Earth."

26
00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:58.066
"When can we leave? I have to say good-bye to my friends, and . . ."

27
00:01:58.067 --> 00:02:04.473
Ally trailed off, noticing Tina's odd expression. "Is something wrong?"

28
00:02:04.474 --> 00:02:12.999
"Yes," Tina said. "During my journey here, I discovered that a Jorgandian was following my ship.

29
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:23.069
I planned to capture it, but I lost track of the life-form after landing on Earth.

30
00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:28.497
I'm still trying to find it—before it identifies you or me."

31
00:02:28.498 --> 00:02:32.472
"Or it evaporates us!" Ally said.

32
00:02:32.473 --> 00:02:41.099
"My Alpha located a Jorgandian life-form in Sandville, but she doesn't know its location or whose body it is occupying.

33
00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:46.159
Alpha is scanning more life-forms today."

34
00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:49.748
"Your Alpha must stop!" Tina said urgently.

35
00:02:49.749 --> 00:02:52.680
"That's why I had to reveal myself to you.

36
00:02:52.681 --> 00:02:57.659
My Alpha notified me that your Alpha was in the diner, out in public. If

37
00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:03.871
the Jorgandian locks onto your Alpha's signal, it will know where to find you!" "Oh

38
00:03:03.872 --> 00:03:12.957
no!" Ally moaned. "I thought I was safe as long as humans are around." "That's

39
00:03:12.958 --> 00:03:22.045
true," Tina said, "but the Jorgandian could find a way to trick you into being alone with it." Ally

40
00:03:22.046 --> 00:03:27.810
shivered. She was still in danger. "Wait!

41
00:03:27.811 --> 00:03:32.886
My Alpha can't do certain things because she's in an Earthling computer. But

42
00:03:32.887 --> 00:03:37.042
why can't your Alpha locate the Jorgandian?" Tina

43
00:03:37.043 --> 00:03:38.983
looked grim. "As

44
00:03:38.984 --> 00:03:50.119
long as a Jorgandian remains inside a human, and doesn't step outdoors, our Astralian technology cannot detect it." "Alpha

45
00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:53.690
never mentioned that!" Ally thought. "I

46
00:03:53.691 --> 00:03:59.792
took the job at the museum hoping I could get Dr. Lloyd's beacon working," Tina said. "Unfortunately,

47
00:03:59.793 --> 00:04:04.073
his experiment is too primitive for—" Ping!

48
00:04:04.074 --> 00:04:07.091
Tina looked at her phone. "It's

49
00:04:07.092 --> 00:04:10.337
Phil. I must get back to the museum. But

50
00:04:10.338 --> 00:04:16.434
I'll be in touch soon. Remember to keep your Alpha powered down for now. The

51
00:04:16.435 --> 00:04:23.919
Jorgandian must not find you!" ***

52
00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:26.939
At home Ally filled in Mateo.

53
00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.664
He was amazed.

54
00:04:28.665 --> 00:04:33.970
"That's great news. But you have to find the Jorgandian!"

55
00:04:33.971 --> 00:04:40.999
"I know." Ally sighed. "Tina's working on it too."

56
00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:44.071
Then Mateo filled her in on Ray's news.

57
00:04:44.072 --> 00:04:49.229
"The CEO definitely wants to expand the diner into a chain of restaurants.

58
00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:54.342
Papi promised to give him an answer by the end of the week."

59
00:04:54.343 --> 00:05:00.563
He looked sad. "It feels like everyone has a big stuff on their minds lately."

60
00:05:00.564 --> 00:05:03.497
"What do you mean?" Ally asked.

61
00:05:03.498 --> 00:05:08.342
Mateo shrugged. "I'm sad about the changes at the diner.

62
00:05:08.343 --> 00:05:12.115
And Coach Cross is having problems too.

63
00:05:12.116 --> 00:05:17.175
His brother has been super busy, and he's acting strangely.

64
00:05:17.176 --> 00:05:24.676
He barely remembers his own name, and he won't step outdoors, not even to go home to sleep."

65
00:05:24.677 --> 00:05:29.852
"Wait . . ." Ally's mouth fell wide open.

66
00:05:29.853 --> 00:05:33.494
"Did you say, he won't leave his shop?"

67
00:05:33.495 --> 00:05:39.832
Mateo nodded, and Ally flashed back to her earlier conversation with Tina.

68
00:05:39.833 --> 00:05:45.075
In fourth grade, Ally hadn't listened to the lesson about Jorgandians.

69
00:05:45.076 --> 00:05:50.852
But earlier today in the alleyway, she'd hung on Tina's every word.

70
00:05:50.853 --> 00:05:54.358
"That's it!" She leaped to her feet.

71
00:05:54.359 --> 00:06:00.953
"I have to call Tina! I know who the Jorgandian is—Eli Cross!"

